course: dictionary
lesson: 6605
title: None: not one, not any
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «None» is a small word that means not one, or not any. If you had ten apples and ate them all, you would have none left. Zero is the number for none, so you can use it in maths too.
explain: When a group is named, use «none of». «Every one of these machines swaps force for distance or speed; none of them gives energy for free.» Here none means not a single machine gives energy for free.
explain: Ask yourself, "How many?" If the answer is zero, the word you need is none. «Families help in different ways, and none of them is wrong.» That means no family is wrong.
fact: None means not one, or not any.
fact: «None of» is used with a group, as in «none of them».
fact: When someone asks "How many?", the answer «None» means zero.
fact: «None of your business» is a rude way to say «that is not for you to know», so do not use it to be unkind.
fact: «Second to none» means the very best, as in «second to none» at football.
exercise: «The jar is empty. How many sweets are left?» | Two | *None | Many | Some
exercise: «Every one of these machines swaps force for distance or speed; none of them gives energy for free.» What does none mean here? | Every one | Most of them | Half of them | *Not a single one
exercise: «Families help in different ways, and none of them is wrong.» Which idea is true? | Some families are wrong | *No family is wrong | Only big families are wrong | Families are always wrong
test: Ben had four pencils and gave them all away. He has none left. What number does none show here? | Four | Ten | One | *Zero
test: Which word means not a single one of a group? | Every | Several | Some | *None of
exam: What does «None of your business» mean? | That is a very good answer | *That is not for you to know | That is a question about money | Please tell me more about it
